   "id": "7d2356f0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Three model types, each given a fair chance\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Logistic regression:** adds up weighted inputs. Simple and easy to explain.\n",
    "- **Random forest:** averages many decision trees, each trained on a random part of the data.\n",
    "- **Gradient boosting:** builds decision trees one after another, each fixing the mistakes of the last.\n",
    "\n",
    "Every model has settings that change how it learns. So that no model loses only because of poor settings, we try a small grid of settings for each and keep the best, judged by average precision."
   ]
  },
