   "source": [
    "def reliability(p, bins=(0, 0.05, 0.10, 0.20, 0.30, 0.45, 0.60, 0.80, 1.0001)):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Average predicted risk against the share that really failed, inside each band of predictions.\"\"\"\n",
    "    band = pd.cut(p, bins=list(bins), right=False)\n",
    "    table = pd.DataFrame({\"predicted\": p, \"failed\": y.to_numpy()}).groupby(band, observed=True)\n",
    "    return table.agg(predicted=(\"predicted\", \"mean\"), observed=(\"failed\", \"mean\"), shipments=(\"failed\", \"size\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = go.Figure()\n",
    "fig.add_trace(go.Scatter(x=[0, 1], y=[0, 1], mode=\"lines\", name=\"Perfectly honest\",\n",
    "                         line=dict(color=MUTED, width=2, dash=\"dash\"), hoverinfo=\"skip\"))\n",
    "for (name, p), color in zip(proba.items(), [BLUE, ORANGE, AQUA]):\n",
    "    table = reliability(p)\n",
    "    fig.add_trace(go.Scatter(\n",
    "        x=table[\"predicted\"], y=table[\"observed\"], mode=\"lines+markers\", name=name,\n",
    "        line=dict(color=color, width=2), marker=dict(size=8, line=dict(color=SURFACE, width=2)),\n",
    "        customdata=table[\"shipments\"],\n",
    "        hovertemplate=name + \"<br>Model said %{x:.0%}<br>Really failed %{y:.0%}<br>Shipments: %{customdata:,}<extra></extra>\",\n",
    "    ))\n",
    "fig.update_xaxes(title_text=\"Risk the model predicted\", tickformat=\".0%\", range=[0, 1.02])\n",
    "fig.update_yaxes(title_text=\"Share that really failed\", tickformat=\".0%\", range=[0, 1.02])\n",
    "style(fig, \"Predicted risk against what happened\", height=500)\n",
    "fig.update_layout(legend=dict(orientation=\"h\", y=-0.2, x=0, font=dict(color=INK)), margin=dict(b=100))\n",
    "fig.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "gap = pd.Series({name: (reliability(p).eval(\"abs(predicted - observed) * shipments\").sum() / len(y))\n",
    "                 for name, p in proba.items()}, name=\"average_gap_between_predicted_and_observed\")\n",
    "gap.round(4).to_frame()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "880e6b92",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**What this tells us:**\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Gradient boosting is the most honest.** On average its percentage is within about half a point of what happened. When it says 70%, about 70% fail.\n",
    "- **Random forest is close**, about 2 points off on average.\n",
    "- **Logistic regression is the least reliable in the middle.** When it says about 50%, roughly three quarters of those shipments fail. It ranks shipments well but its percentages cannot be shown to a coordinator as they are."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2b2623f9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Choose the model\n",
    "\n",
    "We choose with a rule written down before looking at the answer:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Highest average precision wins, because the coordinator works from the top of the list.\n",
    "2. If two models are closer than their round-to-round spread, they are tied on step 1, and the one with the lower Brier score wins, because the app shows the percentage on screen."
   ]
  },
