    "**What this tells us:**\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Same workload, better alerts.** With an identical 505 alerts across the working set, the model's list holds 375 real failures against 339 for the rule of thumb. That is 36 more shipments caught, 22% fewer false alarms, and about $2.3 million more cargo value inside the alerts.\n",
    "- **It still helps when nothing looks wrong.** With the 185 obvious shipments removed, about 12% of the rest fail. The model's average precision there is 0.51 against 0.41 for the rule, and its alerts are right 59% of the time, five times better than picking at random.\n",
    "- **The limit:** at the 30% line the model catches 43% of the not-obvious failures. More than half are still missed. The model gives a coordinator a real head start on shipments that look fine, and it does not see everything."
   ]
  },
